WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.638
IS DISTINCT FROM is useful when you need a definite
comparison between

00:00:03.662 --> 00:00:08.875
nullable values Ordinary equality or inequality can
become UNKNOWN when NULL is

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:14.538
involved IS DISTINCT FROM avoids that uncertainty
Two equal non-NULL

00:00:14.562 --> 00:00:19.000
values are not distinct Two NULL values are also
treated as not

00:00:19.012 --> 00:00:24.700
distinct A NULL compared with a non-NULL value is
distinct The companion

00:00:24.725 --> 00:00:29.925
predicate IS NOT DISTINCT FROM works like NULL-safe
equality Run the example

00:00:29.938 --> 00:00:34.425
and focus on rows containing NULL The output still
contains true or

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.000
false rather than unknown Use these predicates when
missingness is part of

00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:40.350
the comparison itself
